Dialogue: 3,0:01:26.70,0:01:32.45,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIGS. 10–11 · NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE COPY
Dialogue: 3,0:01:26.70,0:01:32.45,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"EARLY AID IN INJURIES AND ACCIDENTS" · FRIEDRICH VON ESMARCH · 1883
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.54,0:01:39.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}His first aid lectures, published in English in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.29,0:01:41.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}1883, described an improvised version.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.51,0:01:44.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A handkerchief tied loosely around the limb, with a
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.50,0:01:46.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}short stick pushed under it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.14,0:01:49.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A walking stick, a door key, even a sword in its sheath.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.41,0:01:51.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The stick was then twisted, round and round.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:36.79,0:01:42.54,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1531 0 l 1531 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:01:36.79,0:01:42.54,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:01:36.79,0:01:42.54,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FIGS. 10–11 · NATIONAL LIBRARY OF MEDICINE COPY
Dialogue: 3,0:01:36.79,0:01:42.54,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"EARLY AID IN INJURIES AND ACCIDENTS" · FRIEDRICH VON ESMARCH · 1883
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.44,0:01:55.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}That twisting stick is the same idea inside a modern
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.83,0:01:56.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}tourniquet.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.55,0:01:58.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Today it's called the windlass.
