Dialogue: 3,0:02:31.73,0:02:36.23,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}WAR DEPARTMENT TRAINING FILM NO. 71 · LISTED AS 1925 · NATIONAL ARCHIVES 111-M-489
Dialogue: 3,0:02:31.73,0:02:36.23,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL ARMY TRAINING FILM · "THE MEDICAL SERVICE WITH INFANTRY IN COMBAT"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.86,0:02:42.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Not everyone agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.18,0:02:45.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Late in the same war, two Army doctors, Wolff and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.40,0:02:48.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Adkins, reported on about 200 wounded service
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.36,0:02:50.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}members who had tourniquets.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.20,0:02:53.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They reported no gangrene, clots, or nerve damage
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.43,0:02:55.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}they could attribute to the devices.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.80,0:02:57.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The fear stayed anyway.
Dialogue: 2,0:02:41.11,0:02:46.86,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1682 0 l 1682 132 l 0 132{\p0}
